      translation: "The Prophet ﷺ said: While I was at the House, between sleep and wakefulness - and he mentioned a man between two men - a golden basin full of wisdom and faith was brought to me. I was cut open from the top of the chest to below the belly, then my belly was washed with the water of Zamzam, then it was filled with wisdom and faith. Then a white animal was brought to me, smaller than a mule and larger than a donkey: al-Buraq. I set off with Jibril until we came to the lowest heaven... [the seven heavens, and the prophets in them] ...Then I was raised to the Lote Tree of the Utmost Boundary: its fruits were like the jars of Hajar and its leaves like the ears of elephants. He said: This is the Lote Tree of the Utmost Boundary. And there were four rivers: two hidden and two visible. I said: What are these, O Jibril? He said: The two hidden are two rivers in Paradise, and the two visible are the Nile and the Euphrates. Then the Frequented House was raised up for me, and a vessel of wine, a vessel of milk and a vessel of honey were brought to me. I took the milk, and he said: It is the natural way that you and your nation are upon. Then the prayers were made obligatory upon me: fifty prayers every day. I returned and passed by Musa, who said: What were you commanded? I said: Fifty prayers every day. He said: Your nation will not be able to bear fifty prayers a day; by Allah, I tried people before you and I strove with the Children of Israel with the utmost striving. Go back to your Lord and ask Him to lighten it for your nation. So I went back, and He took ten from me; I returned to Musa and he said the same; I went back and He took ten from me; I returned to Musa and he said the same; I went back and He took ten from me; I returned to Musa and he said the same; I went back and I was commanded ten prayers every day; I returned and he said the same; I went back and I was commanded five prayers every day. I returned to Musa and he said: What were you commanded? I said: Five prayers every day. He said: Your nation will not be able to bear five prayers a day; I have tried people before you and strove with the Children of Israel with the utmost striving; go back to your Lord and ask Him to lighten it for your nation. I said: I have asked my Lord until I am ashamed; I am content, and I submit. When I passed on, a caller called: I have carried out My obligation, and I have lightened it for My servants.",
